{"step_index":48,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T09:59:34Z","content":"OK, I can see the issues now. Let me explain both clearly:\n\n### Issue 1: The API Key\nThe 401 error means the API key I tried is wrong (it was partially hidden in your screenshot). You need to **click the eye icon** next to your Default Key on the Endpoint page to reveal the full key, then copy it.\n\n### Issue 2: Can you use Fable 5 from Claude Code? ❌ Not yet.\n\nLooking at your third screenshot, the Claude Code provider shows **\"0 connections\"** and **\"No connections yet\"**. The models listed (Opus 5, Fable 5, Sonnet 5, Haiku 4.5) are just showing what *will be available* — but they **won't work until you connect your Claude account**.\n\nTo make it work:\n1. Click **\"+ Add Connection\"** on the Claude Code provider page\n2. It will open an OAuth window — **sign in with your Claude Code account**\n3. Once it shows \"1 connection\", *then* Fable 5 and all other models become usable\n\n### What actually works right now:\nOnly **OpenCode Free** is connected. So you can test with this command — just **replace `YOUR_KEY_HERE`** with your actual full API key from the dashboard:\n\n```powershell\n$body = @{ model = \"oc/cc/claude-opus-5\"; messages = @(@{ role = \"user\"; content = \"Say hello\" }) } | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 3\nInvoke-RestMethod -Uri \"http://localhost:20128/v1/chat/completions\" -Method Post -Headers @{ \"Authorization\" = \"Bearer YOUR_KEY_HERE\"; \"Content-Type\" = \"application/json\" } -Body $body\n```\n\n### Summary:\n\n| Provider | Status | Can you use it? |\n|----------|--------|----------------|\n| **OpenCode Free** | ✅ Ready | Yes — use model `oc/cc/claude-opus-5` |\n| **Claude Code** (Fable 5) | ❌ 0 connections | No — click \"+ Add Connection\" first |\n\nWant me to help you connect the Claude Code provider for Fable 5?","thinking":"The API key I used was partially visible from the screenshot. The actual key is blurred. The 401 error means the API key is wrong. Let me not keep guessing and instead explain to the user what's happening.\n\nAlso, regarding the Claude Code provider - it shows \"0 connections\" which means they can't use Fable 5 directly without first connecting their Claude Code account.\n\nLet me address both issues clearly."}
