{"step_index":78,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T10:08:49Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 1 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. I have downloaded this. Where is it? Find out! What is its work? \n2. Do it by yourself. \n3. Continue, I have removed that item. \n4. Now how can I use Opus 4.5 and all the models present over here? How and here is the list. dnsProviders\nManage your AI provider connections\nsearch\nCustom Providers (OpenAI/Anthropic Compatible)\nextensionNo custom providers — use buttons above to add OpenAI/Anthropic compatible endpoints\nOAuth Providers\n[Claude CodeNo connections](http://localhost:20128/dashboard/providers/claude)[AntigravityNo connections](http://localhost:20128/dashboard/providers/antigravity)[OpenAI CodexNo connections](http://localhost:20128/dashboard/providers/codex)[QoderNo connections](http://localhost:20128/dashboard/providers/qoder)[GitHub CopilotNo connections](http://localhost:20128/dashboard/providers/github)[Cursor IDENo connections](http://localhost:20128/dashboard/providers/cursor)[Kilo CodeNo connections](http://localhost:20128/dashboard/providers/kilocode)[ClineNo connections](http://localhost:20128/dashboard/providers/cline)[ClinePassNo connections](http://localhost:20128/dashboard/providers/clinepass)[CodeBuddyNo connec\n<truncated 4855 bytes>\n5. I have added Opus 4.6 here in open code free. Can we use it? \n6. I have copied this to power cell and it's writing something else. I have given you two screenshots. And I have given you another provider cloud board to use faber 5. Can we use it directly faber 5? \n7. So I have added in Open Code Free the Fable 5 too. Can we use it now and use opus 4.5 that is ready to give me the answer and tell me how I can just use all the time opus 5 so my credits don't go out? My tokens can be saved and I can use that opus 5. \n8. It is writing this. Am I pasting it right or you can tell me? Are we using Opus 5 or not? Just tell me in which model I am talking \n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n**Request A: Use Opus 5 / Fable 5 for free via 9Router OpenCode Free — IMPLEMENTATION**\n- User's intent: \"tell me how I can just use all the time opus 5 so my credits don't go out? My tokens can be saved and I can use that opus 5\"\n- User added `oc/cc/claude-opus-5` and `oc/cc/claude-fable-5` models to the OpenCode Free provider in 9Router dashboard\n- API key was found from the database: `sk-700204ea6f63961f-y3q6mu-672260ea`\n- The `/v1/models` endpoint returns 200 and lists both `oc/cc/claude-opus-5` and `oc/cc/claude-fable-5` as available models\n- However, the `/v1/chat/completions` endpoint returns **401 Unauthorized** when trying to actually use the models — this is the UNRESOLVED blocker\n- The 401 on chat completions but 200 on models listing is puzzling and needs further debugging\n\n**Request B: Can Fable 5 be used directly? — NOT FULLY ANSWERED**\n- User asked: \"Can we use it directly faber 5?\"\n- Fable 5 was added to OpenCode Free provider, same status as Opus 5 above\n- Claude Code provider shows \"0 connections\" — user has NOT connected any Claude Code OAuth account\n- Only OpenCode Free is the active provider\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n\n- User is `renu5` on Windows, working from `C:\\Users\\renu5`\n- User installed 9Router globally via `npm install -g 9router` — version 0.5.55\n- User is NOT very technical — they literally pasted `\"PASTE_YOUR_FULL_API_KEY_HERE\"` as their API key when I gave placeholder text. Instructions must be extremely explicit and copy-paste ready.\n- User is currently talking to me through **Antigravity IDE** using **Claude Opus 4.6 (Thinking)** model — this is separate from 9Router\